ghpull:740 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "owl_xml_parser: parse nested <Annotation> into meta-annotations (#710)" ;
    bl:number 740 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:710 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr740 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:710 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-30T23:12:33Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-30T23:15:25Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr740Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #710 asked owl_xml_parser's parse_annotation to accept a nested <Annotation> child (a meta-annotation, per the spec's annotationAnnotations := { Annotation } grammar) and thread it into owl_ontology::Annotation::annotations, replacing the stopgap 'not representable (see #695)' error PR #709 left in place while #608 (OWL/XML ABox axioms) was mid-flight on the same file. With #608 merged, the blocker was gone. The fix mirrors owl_functional_parser's annotation() exactly: recognize an 'Annotation' child tag, recurse parse_annotation on it, and build the result with Annotation::with_meta instead of Annotation::new. The implementation was written before its tests (a deviation from this repo's stated TDD order, acknowledged rather than hidden), then covered by unit tests for one- and two-level nesting plus an integration test through the public parse() entrypoint on an axiom-level annotation. A stale-docs sweep (prompted by advisor review) found three other places -- docs/plans/OWL_META_ANNOTATIONS_695_PLAN.md's per-crate table, docs/plans/OWL_XML_PLAN.md's deferred-work note, and CLAUDE.md's owl_xml_parser architecture paragraph -- that still described owl_xml_parser as always-empty/blocked on #695, and updated them to describe the current behavior instead of leaving status language to drift." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:740 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr740 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr740Decision .

session:pr740Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "The child-tag match loop in parse_annotation does not enforce that a nested <Annotation> child precede the <AnnotationProperty>/value children -- it accepts 'Annotation' anywhere among the element's children and simply appends to the meta list, the same order-lax approach the existing loop already used for property vs. value. This keeps the change minimal and consistent with the rest of the function rather than adding separate ordered-prefix parsing." ;
    agp:alternative "Could have required meta-annotations to appear strictly before AnnotationProperty/value (closer to the spec's listed production order) by splitting the child iteration into a leading-Annotation-collection phase followed by a property/value phase, as split_axiom_annotations already does for axiom-level annotations. Rejected as unnecessary complexity: no OWL/XML producer is known to emit <Annotation> children out of spec order, and the existing single-pass loop already tolerates property/value in either order with no reported issues." .
